/// The Very Small Pet Shop ///

The Very Small Pet Shop is a whimsical, interactive pet adoption experience where
the pets choose you.

Meet six fun and spirited pets, complete a personality questionaire, and see if
your personality is compatible with theirs. Each pet has their own preferences,
expectations, and dealbreakers (and might reject you based on them)!

/// Features ///

    - Interactive pet shop: Explore six unique pets, each with their own personality, 
    profile, and preferences.

    - Personality questionnaire: Complete a scenario-based questionnaire evaluating 
    four personality traits: Sociability, Persistence, Patience, and Spontaneity.

    - Compatibility engine: Receive personalized compatibility scores calculated using 
    weighted personality comparisons.

    - Dealbreaker system: Certain preferences are non-negotiable. A high compatibility 
    score doesn't guarantee acceptance!

    - Personality comparisons: Compare your personality traits against historical 
    applicants using percentile calculations.

    - Adoption experience: Adopt an accepting pet and bring your new companion home.

    - Design: Custom illustrations, animated pet sprites, interactive profiles, and
    transitions bring the experience to life.

/// Compatiblity Engine ///

Each pet has an ideal personality profile, individual trait weights, and unique 
acceptance requirements.

    - Personality scoring: Questionnaire responses contribute points to one or more 
    personality traits.

    - Normalization: Raw personality scores are normalized to a consistent 0–10 scale.

    - Weighted compatibility: Each pet's ideal personality profile is compared against 
    the applicant's profile, with trait weights determining the importance of each 
    difference.

    - Dealbreaker evaluation: Specific answers can trigger hard rejection conditions, 
    regardless of the overall compatibility score.

    - Acceptance decision: Each pet has its own acceptance threshold, producing 
    individualized adoption decisions.

/// Personality Percentiles ///

Applicants can also see how their personality compares with previous applicants.

The backend stores normalized personality scores in PostgreSQL and calculates 
percentiles from historical application data. This allows applicants to see how 
they rank across all four personality traits.

Percentiles are calculated using database queries against previously submitted 
applications rather than being stored as fixed values.

/// Tech Stack ///

Frontend
    - React
    - Javascript
    - Vite
    - CSS

Backend
    - Python
    - FastAPI
    - SQLAlchemy
    - PostgreSQL

/// Downloading the Project ///

Prereqs

    - Node.js and npm
    - Python 3.10+
    - PostgreSQL

Clone the Repo

    git clone https://github.com/erinkim789/Very-Small-Pet-Shop.git
    cd very-small-pet-shop

Configure Environmental Variables

Frontend

    Create frontend/.env: VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8000 -> URL of the FastAPI backend

Backend

    Create backend/.env: DATABASE_URL=postgresql://username:password@localhost:5432/database_name -> Replaced the example credentials and database name with your backend configuration

Set Up the Backend

    Create and activate the virtual environment: 
        - python -m venv .venv
        - source .venv/bin/activate

    Install backend dependencies: 
        - pip install -r backend/requirements.txt

Initialize the Database

    Make sure your PostgreSQL server is running and the .env file is correctly set up for the backend

    Run the database seeding script:
        - python -m backend.seed_data

    The seed script populates the data with sample historical applications. This is important for the personality
    percentile comparisons to have existing applicant data to compare against

Start the Backend

    From the project root:
        - uvicorn backend.application:app --reload
    
    The API will be available at http://localhost:8000

Start the Frontend

    Open a separate terminal:
        - cd frontend
        - npm install
        - npm run dev

    Vite will provide the local frontend URL in the terminal.

